    "sentence_translations": [
      "Spring Sleepiness",
      "",
      "Annie is calling Little Ming.",
      "",
      "Annie: Hi Little Ming, get up! We should leave for the spring outing.",
      "",
      "Little Ming: No, I’m too sleepy. You guys can go. Let me sleep some more.",
      "",
      "Annie: Don’t sleep. It is finally spring and starting to get warm. It’s time to go outside.",
      "",
      "Little Ming: I’m sleepy because of spring. Haven’t you heard about “spring sleepiness”?",
      "",
      "Annie: What’s spring sleepiness? I feel like you are sleepy all year round.",
      "",
      "Little Ming: It is quite common.",
      "“Sleepy in spring, tired in autumn, taking a nap in summer, can’t stay awake for the three winter months.”",
      "You see? Even ancient people had these sayings.",
      "",
      "Annie: Obviously it’s just because you are lazy. Don’t use ancient people as an excuse.",
      "",
      "Little Ming: Ok, don’t nag me any more. I’ll get up.",
      "",
      "Annie: That’s right. Take a walk outdoors and you won’t feel sleepy!",
      ""
    ]
  }
